<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine YPF against sale to competitors.</title>
<headline>Argentine YPF against sale to competitors.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil firm YPF SA would oppose any government move to sell a big block of its remaining 20-percent share to another international oil company, YPF president Nells Leon said late Monday</p>
<p>In a statement to the local National Securities Commission, Leon said &quot;placing a considerable packet of shares with one of...international competitors would be inconsistent with the objectives of privatization adopted by the government in the moment of the initial public offer.&quot;</p>
<p>The government said recently it is studying the possibility of selling YPF shares. It sold most of the company in 1993.</p>
<p>Leon's comments came after recent Argentine press reports that Spanish company Repsol was interested in buying into YPF.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
